6. h3 { Stops ...Bg4, which would pin the knight on f3 to the queen. } ( 6. O-O a6 ) ( 6. Be3 Bxe3 { Trades the bishops, so White's pawns on e3 and f2 are doubled after fxe3. } 7. fxe3 O-O ) ( 6. Ng5 O-O { Nxf7 would cost White the knight and bishop for a rook, so Black castles and ignores the knight. } 7. O-O Bg4 { Develops with a hit on the queen. White must move it before trying anything on f7, and Black then plays ...h6. } 8. Qe1 h6 ) ( 6. Na4 Bb6 { Keeps the bishop. If the knight takes on b6, the a-pawn recaptures and the rook on a8 gets the open a-file. } 7. Nxb6 axb6 ) 6... a6 { The usual plan: the bishop gets a retreat on a7, then Black castles. } 7. O-O { The same position as after 5.O-O d6 6.d3 a6 7.h3. } ( 7. a3 O-O ) ( 7. Be3 Bxe3 8. fxe3 O-O ) 7... O-O *
